---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AboutSection from "../components/AboutSection.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Home:Life's Little Things">
	<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 pt-10">
		<div class="rounded-lg border-2 border-secondary bg-white p-6 shadow-sm text-text">
			<h1 class="text-3xl font-title text-primary mb-3">Business Disclosures</h1>
			<p class="font-description leading-relaxed">Life's Little Things is a trade name of Eshe M. Snow.</p>
			<p class="font-description leading-relaxed">Mailing address: 18 Newlyn Ln, Bella Vista, AR 72715.</p>
			<p class="font-description leading-relaxed">Contact: <a class="text-primary hover:underline" href="mailto:lltcrafts22@gmail.com">lltcrafts22@gmail.com</a></p>
		</div>
	</section>
	<AboutSection 
		title="A Little About Me"
		paragraphs={[
			"Hi, I’m Eshe Snow. I currently live in Russellville, Arkansas, and frequently travel back and forth between there and Bentonville. I’ve been happily married to my husband Brady since October 2025.",
			"I’m a proud introvert who finds joy in a variety of creative hobbies, including jewelry making, painting, baking, and — my absolute favorite — crocheting. When I’m not working on a crochet project, you’ll often find me playing video games or experimenting in the kitchen."
		]}
		image="/About/IMG_20260430_203445.jpg"
		align="left">
	</AboutSection>
	<AboutSection 
		title="My Crochet Journey"
		paragraphs={[
			"I began crocheting about three years ago after discovering it through Instagram Reels. Like many of my hobbies, I decided to give it a try, and my very first project was a small bee. While the result left me somewhat discouraged (it was much more challenging than the videos made it appear), I wasn’t ready to give up.",
			"As I continued practicing and experimenting with different projects, I discovered my true passion: amigurumi. Growing up, I was always drawn to stuffed animals, and the joy of bringing them to life with my own hands quickly became addictive. The more I created, the more I wanted to share that joy with others.",
			"What started as free gifts for friends and family soon turned into frequent commissions. After realizing how expensive yarn can be, I decided it was time to turn my passion into a small business. That’s how Life’s Little Things was born."
		]}
		image="/About/IMG_20260430_203450.jpg"
		align="right">
	</AboutSection>
	<AboutSection 
		title="The Business Story"
		paragraphs={[
			'I chose the name Life’s Little Things because my name, Eshe, means “Life” in Swahili. It felt like a beautiful and personal way to brand my work — essentially “Eshe’s Little Things.',
			'I’m constantly inspired with new ideas, which keeps the creative process exciting and helps me sustain and grow the business.'
		]}
		image="/About/IMG_20260430_203456.jpg"
		align="left">
	</AboutSection>
	<AboutSection 
		title="Inspiration & Process"
		paragraphs={[
			"Most of my inspiration comes from Pinterest and Instagram. However, I rarely follow a pattern exactly as written. I enjoy adding my own creative touches to make each piece unique.",
			"My process usually begins with selecting the perfect yarn colors, then starting with the head, followed by the body, limbs, and finally the details that bring the character to life. Custom commissions are especially fun — I love taking familiar designs and personalizing them with special accessories or unique requests."
		]}
		image="/About/IMG_20260430_215843.jpg"
		align="right">
	</AboutSection>
	<AboutSection 
		title="Personal Touches"
		paragraphs={[
			"I’ve never been one to follow the crowd or copy others. Instead, I take pride in putting my own spin on every piece I create. I’m a bit of a perfectionist, and I pour careful time and attention into each project. There’s nothing more rewarding than seeing the smile on a customer’s face when their vision comes to life.",
			"I primarily use soft, chunky Bernat Blanket Yarn for my stuffed animals because of its luxurious feel and durability. For smaller items like keychains, I typically use acrylic yarn, which is more budget-friendly and allows one skein to go a long way.",
			"My goal is simple: to create pieces that bring as much happiness to my customers as they bring to me while making them."
		]}
		image="/About/IMG_20260430_203447.jpg"
		align="left">
	</AboutSection>
	<AboutSection 
		title="My Mission"
		paragraphs={[
			"I love being a small business owner because it allows me to connect with people on a personal level while doing something I’m truly passionate about.",
			"Life's Little Things is dedicated to creating stuffies and other handcrafted pieces to remind people that the little things matter most. - Handmade with love and care in every stitch."
		]}
		image="/About/IMG_20260430_203459.jpg"
		align="right">
	</AboutSection>
</BaseLayout>
